WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.582
The kit's login plan reads one
instance from the audit snapshot,

2
00:00:03.582 --> 00:00:04.988
and the reviewed mapping.

3
00:00:04.988 --> 00:00:08.351
It leaves out the S A account
and the built-in principals.

4
00:00:08.351 --> 00:00:12.488
A login with no mapping is written
as unresolved, instead of a guess.

5
00:00:12.488 --> 00:00:15.022
It mirrors server and database roles,

6
00:00:15.022 --> 00:00:18.701
and writes three scripts:
create, cutover and rollback.

7
00:00:18.701 --> 00:00:20.188
It executes nothing.

8
00:00:20.188 --> 00:00:24.333
It also warns when a principal would
hold more than one database role,

9
00:00:24.333 --> 00:00:27.969
or D B owner or sys-admin, because
the data platform book gives

10
00:00:27.969 --> 00:00:31.750
each group exactly one role, on
one database, in one environment.

11
00:00:31.750 --> 00:00:33.825
A warning doesn't stop the plan.

12
00:00:33.825 --> 00:00:37.925
It's for the identity engineer to
split the group, or record why not.

13
00:00:37.925 --> 00:00:40.863
What the plan doesn't mirror
is explicit permissions,

14
00:00:40.863 --> 00:00:43.000
default schemas and object ownership.

15
00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:47.400
Runbook R five's queries read those,
and the D B A adds them by hand.
